</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> When the price is \($5\) per download, what is the number of downloads in thousands? </item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(13\)</para>
  </list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> When the price is \($10\) per download, what is the number of downloads in thousands? </item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(8\)</para>
  </list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> When the price is \($12\) per download, what is the number of downloads in thousands? </item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(6\)</para>
  </list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item> When the price is \($15\) per download, what is the number of downloads in thousands? </item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(3\)</para>
  </list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item> When the price is \($18\) per download, what is the number of downloads in thousands? </item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0\)</para>
  </list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
    <item> When the price is \($x\) per download, what is the number of downloads in thousands? </item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(18-x\)</para>
  </list>
</list>
<para> For 7 - 12 complete the table by finding the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">revenue</term> at each price. The first row has been completed for you.</para>


<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
